\f1\fs22 \'93Oh, tax!\'94 the contract killer type cursed. \'93It\'92s her. The one.\'94\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Yeah, creepy,
\f1\i0  Sarah thought, ignoring his slack-jaw stare.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There you are, Mr Fairy Boxers,\'94 she said, ambushing Chanta from behind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta ejected from his chair and attempted a mid-air half-turn. His clumsiness shoved the chair at Sarah; she caught it easily, spun it back, and slid it under him. \'93Sit, relax,\'94 she said, planting her hands on his shoulders.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta stifled an ecstatic moan.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s polite smile chilled as she locked eyes with Halo. \'93I\'92m Sarah. Tony, introduce me to your friends.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta tried mouthing some words, then decided not mouthing words would be wiser. Then he tried both simultaneously, achieving equal paralysis. His three friends sprang up with awkward handshakes and unsteady introductions.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo frightened Sarah. \'93What big eyes you have,\'94 she said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo\'92s nerves turned to steel. \'93All the better to see you with, my dear.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Tony, honey.\'94 Sarah kissed Chanta\'92s cheek\'97affectionate, familiar. \'93We\'92ll be late for dinner.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She helped him stand and looped her arm around him, broadcasting brand-new romance. Chanta, weak-kneed, leaned into her embrace and shuffled like he\'92d only recently discovered walking.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Abe whistled. Major nodded. Halo watched until Sarah disappeared in the crowd. It wasn\'92t just beauty\'97she glowed with the kind of vitality Halo ached for. \'93Stacy bitch,\'94 he muttered.\
